# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# This is a .gitignore file, which tells Git which files and directories to ignore and not track in version control. Each section targets different types of files or directories that are commonly excluded from source control. 

# Logs: This section ignores log files, which are typically generated during the build and runtime processes.
# logs: Ignores any directory named logs.
# *.log: Ignores all files with the .log extension.
# npm-debug.log*, yarn-debug.log*, yarn-error.log*, pnpm-debug.log*, lerna-debug.log*: Ignores specific debug and error log files generated by npm, yarn, pnpm, and lerna.


# Build Artifacts and Dependencies: This section ignores directories and files related to dependencies and build artifacts.
# node_modules: Ignores the node_modules directory where Node.js packages are installed.
# dist: Ignores the dist directory typically used for compiled or bundled output.
# dist-ssr: Ignores the dist-ssr directory used for server-side rendering build output.
# *.local: Ignores all files with the .local extension, often used for local configuration files.


# Editor Directories and Files: This section ignores configuration files and directories generated by various code editors and IDEs.
# .vscode/*: Ignores all files in the .vscode directory except for extensions.json.
# !.vscode/extensions.json: An exception that ensures extensions.json in the .vscode directory is tracked by Git.
# .idea: Ignores the .idea directory, which is used by JetBrains IDEs like IntelliJ IDEA and WebStorm.
# .DS_Store: Ignores .DS_Store files, which are created by macOS to store custom attributes of a folder.
# *.suo: Ignores solution user option files created by Visual Studio.
# *.ntvs*, *.njsproj, *.sln: Ignores project files and solutions created by Visual Studio.
# *.sw?: Ignores swap files created by the Vim editor (e.g., .swp, .swo).

